---
import PageShell from '../components/PageShell.astro';

const title = 'About AITokenCalculator — Free AI Token & API Cost Estimator';
const description =
  'AITokenCalculator is a free, browser-based AI token and cost calculator covering 51 models from nine providers. Learn who builds it, why it exists, and how it stays accurate.';

const published = '2026-08-21T00:00:00Z';
---

<PageShell
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path="/about/"
  publishedTime={published}
  modifiedTime={published}
  eyebrow="About"
  heading="About AITokenCalculator"
  lead="A fast, honest way to answer one question every LLM developer asks: what will this prompt actually cost me?"
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h2>What is AITokenCalculator?</h2>
    <p>
      AITokenCalculator is a <strong>free, browser-based token and cost calculator</strong> for
      AI APIs. It covers <strong>51 models from nine providers</strong> — OpenAI, Anthropic,
      Google, Mistral, Meta, xAI, DeepSeek, MiniMax and Moonshot — including text, image, audio
      and multi-turn chat workloads.
    </p>
    <p>
      Paste text to get an instant token estimate, pick any model to see its real pricing
      applied, project monthly spend at your request volume, compare up to three models side by
      side, or rank the entire catalog by cost for your exact workload. Caching discounts, batch
      mode and reasoning-token multipliers are all built in.
    </p>

    <h2>Why we built it</h2>
    <p>
      Every pricing page shows rates per million tokens; almost nobody thinks in those units.
      The questions that actually matter — "what does this feature cost per month?", "is Claude
      cheaper than GPT-4o for my workload?" — require math nobody wants to do in a spreadsheet.
      We wanted one tool that answers in seconds, without signup walls or dark patterns.
    </p>

    <h2>How it stays honest</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Runs entirely in your browser.</strong> Nothing you type ever leaves your device — no accounts, no tracking, no uploads.</li>
      <li><strong>Verified pricing.</strong> Rates are checked against official provider pages on a regular cadence; every page shows its verification date.</li>
      <li><strong>Transparent method.</strong> Our <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a> documents exactly how estimates are computed, including the limitations.</li>
      <li><strong>Estimates, not billing.</strong> We say it everywhere: always confirm final prices with the provider.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What's next</h2>
    <p>
      Deeper workload presets (RAG pipelines, agent loops), exportable reports, and keeping pace
      with the fastest-moving pricing landscape in software. Have an idea?
      <a href="/contact/">Tell us</a> — the best features here started as messages.
    </p>
  </article>
